local E = ns.DB.entries
E["quest:96395"] = {t="quest",n="An Ancient Grudge",z="hallofthanes",s="Deep within the historic Hall of Thanes, an ethereal attendant pleads for an end to the torment of a fallen ruler. The spirit of Faldrim Anvilmar lingers on, consumed by an old grievance and denied eternal peace. Adventurers are tasked with putting the restless thane to rest.",h="Deep within the historic Hall of Thanes, an ethereal attendant pleads for an end to the torment of a fallen...",sec={{t="A Plea From the Grave",b="Within the stone vaults of the Hall of Thanes, death offers no immediate respite. A ghostly attendant of Faldrim Anvilmar lingers there, barely able to muster the strength to speak across the mortal veil. Rather than seeking freedom for itself, the phantom's only concern is its master, begging travelers to quiet the turbulent spirit of the thane.",sp=0},{t="The Weight of the Past",b="Death has not freed Faldrim Anvilmar from the past. Bound to the physical world by a consuming, ancient grudge, Faldrim's ghost remains agitated and hostile, unable to find slumber until granted a forceful release.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Faldrim Anvilmar?",a="Faldrim Anvilmar was a dwarven thane whose restless apparition now haunts the Hall of Thanes. His Ghostly Attendant says he is consumed by an ancient grudge and can find no rest. The quest says nothing more about his life or lineage.",al={"faldrim anvilmar lore","who is faldrim","thane anvilmar"}},{q="Where is the Hall of Thanes located?",a="The Hall of Thanes lies in the caverns beneath Old Ironforge, inside the dwarven capital of Ironforge.",al={"hall of thanes location","where is hall of thanes","hall of thanes entrance"}},{q="Why is the ghost of Faldrim Anvilmar hostile?",a="According to the ghostly attendant, the former thane is consumed by an ancient grudge. Dwarven history is steeped in centuries of clan rivalries, and Faldrim's lingering hatred prevents his spirit from departing into peaceful slumber.",al={"why is faldrim angry","why is thane attacking","ancient grudge explanation"}},{q="Who gives the quest An Ancient Grudge?",a="The quest is bestowed by a Ghostly Attendant found inside the Hall of Thanes. Bound in servitude even after death, the attendant seeks only peace for its former master.",al={"who starts ancient grudge","ghostly attendant quest","quest giver"}},{q="What must you do to complete the quest?",a="You must confront the spirit of Faldrim Anvilmar within the Hall of Thanes, defeat his restless ghost in combat to release him from his torment, and report back to the Ghostly Attendant.",al={"how to finish ancient grudge","put faldrim to rest","ancient grudge objective"}},{q="Is Faldrim related to the town of Anvilmar?",a="That isn't known yet. Faldrim shares his name with the settlement of Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley, but the quest says nothing about his family or any tie to the town.",al={"is faldrim from anvilmar","anvilmar coldridge connection","anvilmar family"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, confronting a restless thane of their own people is a sobering reminder that an ancient grudge can outlast death itself.",["class:Priest"]="Priests understand that lingering grudges and unatoned sorrow can bind a mortal spirit to the physical realm long after the body has turned to dust.",["class:Paladin"]="Laying a tormented soul to rest is a solemn duty for holy warriors sworn to bring peace to the suffering dead."},kw={"ancient grudge","anvilmar","dwarf ghost","faldrim anvilmar","ghostly attendant","hall of thanes","restless spirit","thane"},rel={"zone:hallofthanes","subzone:anvilmar"},m={level="15",id=96395},src={"In-game quest text: An Ancient Grudge"},fv=true}
E["zone:hallofthanes"] = {t="dungeon",n="Hall of Thanes",z="hallofthanes",s="Deep beneath the bustling city of Ironforge lies the Hall of Thanes, an ancient subterranean complex steeped in dwarven history. Intended for early Alliance adventurers, this secluded dungeon holds relics of the mountain kingdom's past that have fallen into peril. Gaining entry requires unearthing forgotten routes through the mountain itself.",h="Deep beneath the bustling city of Ironforge lies the Hall of Thanes, an ancient subterranean complex steeped...",sec={{t="Secrets Beneath the Mountain",b="While Ironforge hums with the ringing of hammers in the Great Forge, forgotten halls delve far deeper beneath the stone. The Hall of Thanes represents one of these venerable subterranean reaches. Long tied to ancestral dwarven bloodlines and relics of stonecraft, it now requires intrepid Alliance champions to venture into its shadowed vaults to secure the depths.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Path",b="Accessing the Hall of Thanes is no casual feat. The corridors leading to these ancient vaults have been sealed away or hidden from everyday travelers in Ironforge. Adventurers must decipher forgotten charting, beginning with recovering an Underground Map, before they can navigate the deeper tunnels and breach the threshold of the dungeon.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Dirgehammer",b="Within the heart of the complex lies a formidable assembly of threats, from enchanted guardians like Plunder and the fiery brute Magmatus to rogue figures of ancient dwarven lineage such as Faldrim Anvilmar. Presiding over the inner sanctuary is Durgen Dirgehammer, whose defeat finally quells the growing unrest simmering beneath the city floor and secures the sacred dwarven halls from subversion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Hall of Thanes located?",a="The Hall of Thanes is located beneath the dwarven capital of Ironforge. It is tucked away in the mountain's deeper, restricted subterranean sectors rather than the main city thoroughfares.",al={"hall of thanes location","where is hall of thanes","ironforge dungeon location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do I gain access to the Hall of Thanes?",a="Entry requires unlocking the dungeon through an attunement questline. Adventurers must begin by pursuing the quest 'Underground Map' to chart a path into the mountain's lower vaults.",al={"how to get into hall of thanes","hall of thanes attunement","underground map quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What bosses are inside the Hall of Thanes?",a="The expedition challenges four major threats: Faldrim Anvilmar, the volcanic behemoth Magmatus, an enchanted golem named Plunder, and the final adversary, Durgen Dirgehammer.",al={"boss list","who are the bosses","hall of thanes bosses"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="What level range is recommended for this dungeon?",a="The dungeon is tailored for Alliance adventurers between levels 13 and 18, serving as an early subterranean challenge alongside Ironforge's deep network.",al={"what level is hall of thanes","hall of thanes level range"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Can Horde players enter the Hall of Thanes?",a="No. The Hall of Thanes is an Alliance-exclusive dungeon situated directly beneath the Alliance capital of Ironforge.",al={"can horde do hall of thanes","is hall of thanes alliance only"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What does defeating Durgen Dirgehammer achieve?",a="Overcoming Durgen Dirgehammer breaks the grip of rogue dwarven forces and their summoned constructs deep within Ironforge's foundations. Striking him down restores safety to the ancient ancestral vaults beneath the Great Forge.",al={"why kill dirgehammer","final boss story","durgen dirgehammer lore"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Hall of Thanes?",a="The Hall of Thanes is an instanced dungeon deep beneath the dwarf capital of Ironforge. While Ironforge usually bustles as the grand home of the Bronzebeard clan, this subterranean domain harbors brewing internal threats and hostile encounters, requiring seasoned defenders of the Alliance to delve beneath the mountain and restore order.",al={"hall of thanes lore","what is this dungeon","hall of thanes dungeon"},it="place",add="89d0670c"},{q="How did I end up in the Hall of Thanes?",a="You followed the trail of an ancient subterranean map uncovered deep within dwarven territory. After unraveling its secrets and gaining access from within Ironforge, your search led you into these forgotten stone halls carved directly under the mountain.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","how did i find the hall of thanes"},it="arrival",add="20f1c0f0"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in the Hall of Thanes?",a="You are here to venture deep into these ancestral vaults, overcome the hostile forces holding them, and strike down the threats lurking in the dark. Your expedition culminates in confronting dangerous renegades and guardians, including Faldrim Anvilmar, Plunder, Magmatus, and Durgen Dirgehammer.",al={"what am i doing here","why am i here","what is my goal here"},it="purpose",add="b863ae36"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, entering the Hall of Thanes is a journey into the ancestral bedrock of Dun Morogh, purging defilers from sacred halls that bear legendary clan names.",["faction:Alliance"]="The stability of Ironforge directly bolsters the Alliance, making the cleansing of these deep caverns vital to securing the High Seat.",["race:Gnome"]="As close allies living within Ironforge, gnomes share an urgent interest in neutralizing mechanical constructs like Plunder that threaten their shared refuge."},kw={"attunement","dungeon","durgen dirgehammer","faldrim anvilmar","hall of thanes","ironforge","magmatus","plunder","underground map"},rel={"zone:ironforge","quest:96391","subzone:anvilmar","topic:alliance"},m={levels="13-18"},src={"Hall of Thanes (instance)"}}
